contentText:
Growing up in the Bronx, Cardi B has been in her fair share of brawls over the years. While enjoying a late-night dinner with her eldest two children, Kulture and Wave, the rapper joked about how they need to learn how to fight to protect their Grammy-winning mother when she can&#8217;t defend herself anymore.

Cardi revealed on Tuesday&#8217;s (Aug. 18) IG Live that she signed up 8-year-old Kulture and 4-year-old Wave for boxing classes, as the rapper wants her children to also be able to protect themselves.

&#8220;This that age when you need to learn how to fight &#8230; Never know when a b&#8212;h gon&#8217; try you when you grow up and s&#8211;t because you in them white, good schools, but you know you outside,&#8221; she explained. &#8220;I ain&#8217;t going to be there for you all the time.&#8221;

Cardi continued: &#8220;And I got some b&#8212;hes that I don’t like, so when you 25 and s&#8211;t and b&#8212;hes f&#8211;k with me? You know I&#8217;m like, ‘Yeah, b&#8212;h. Don&#8217;t make me bring out my daughter. Which daughter you want? Which daughter?&#8221;

The hitmaker made Wave and Kulture laugh when Cardi joked about how she&#8217;s going to need the kids to back her up when she&#8217;s in an argument at senior bingo night. &#8220;When I&#8217;m an old b&#8212;h and I can&#8217;t fight no more, you got me?&#8221; Cardi asked, and Kulture agreed.

“When I&#8217;m like about 60 and I&#8217;m talking s&#8211;t to these b&#8212;hes, that&#8217;s when you come in. &#8216;Kulture, come beat this b&#8212;h ass,&#8221; Cardi said in an elderly accent. &#8220;Yeah, she f&#8211;ked with me. I&#8217;m playing bingo. Yeah, I&#8217;m at bingo and this b&#8212;h f&#8211;king with me. Come over here and bring Blossom too. You&#8217;re going to jump ass.&#8221;

Before cutting off the IG Live, Cardi opened up about Kulture developing a lot of the traits and tendencies that she herself had growing up as a young girl, including not wanting to eat much because she &#8220;hated chewing.&#8221;

It&#8217;s been an action-filled few weeks for Cardi as she closed out July and the first half of August. She picked up her fourth Diamond plaque with &#8220;WAP,&#8221; released her &#8220;AH HA&#8221; single (which reached No. 25 on the Billboard Hot 100 ) and reignited her feud with BIA.
